# E-364 p. 5, section 2D: "Upper case numbers on the Flexowriter appear as
# exponents ... Some examples are"
#
# Run in this order the examples do not finish. b is 1/529, ab³ is about
# 1.7·10⁻⁷, and its fifth power is about 10⁻³⁴: smaller than the 24, 6 system
# can hold (2⁻⁶⁴ is about 5·10⁻²⁰), so it becomes zero, and (ab³)⁻⁵ divides
# by it. The manual gives them as notation, not as a program.
a = 5²,
b = (a - 2)⁻²,
c = (ab³)⁻⁵,
d = a(b + c)²/(c - a)a⁻³,
PRINT a, b, c, d.
100 PRINT a, b.
STOP
